saying I shouldn't make a magical character. I understand this is Hunter &amp; about humans fighting against the odds without supernatural power, but within our group we have a Priest with Benedictions &amp; a Witch with Gnosis 5, I'm not overreaching the power level &amp; I'd like to add a bit of pop to his faith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","name":"Aermas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2266_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"128"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T10:03:49-08:00","id":73771,"title":"","content":"A fair question.<br /> <br /> To me magic is mostly very hard to learn. It's on the level of advanced theoretical mathematics. There are exceptions like Benedictions where anyone can learn but they're rare and valuable, which is why Conspiracies guard them jealously.<br /> <br /> As a stoner who practices new age Druidism, I just don't see how he got hold of genuine magic. That little snippet of info doesn't suggest to me that he put in the years of study to learn magic or is part of a group with the power to acquire and protect an Endowment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T14:33:59-08:00","id":73888,"title":"","content":"For me it's not a balance issue, it's that the way you wrote your comment gave me the impression that you were giving the character magic simply because the character was into new age Druidism and that seemed kinda odd. I mean, there are plenty of neo-pagans around, that doesn't give them magic powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}